    "field": "Pollen-based climate reconstruction",
    "problem": "The proliferation of diverse methods for reconstructing climate from pollen data, each with potential biases and uncertainties, creates a need for a standardized inter-comparison to establish best practices and improve the reliability of climate assessments.",
    "method": "The Pollen-Climate Methods Inter-comparison Project proposes developing standardized fossil and modern pollen datasets to allow for a direct \"bench-test\" comparison between current climate reconstruction methods and to establish best practices for their use.",
    "task": "The task is to compare and review different methods for quantitatively reconstructing past climates from fossil pollen data to improve collaboration, establish best practices, and guide future development within the pollen-climate community.",
